+ ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
+ Carvetto sample post: a multi-spindle drill bank on LinuxCNC, millimetres
+ Written for Carvetto from scratch (clean-room). Licensed with Carvetto.
+ T-0335, ADR-0111. A TEMPLATE to adapt, not a post for a machine as it is.
+
+ It is the shipped LinuxCNC (mm) post plus the five drill bank blocks. The
+ M codes of those blocks (M101 .. M104) are user-defined M codes
+ (LinuxCNC's M100..M199 range): the machine's own macros must implement them
+ for the head it has. Nothing here is a statement about a real head.
+
+ What the blocks mean (ADR-0111). A drill bank toolpath moves the head's
+ reference spindle; [X] [Y] are that spindle's place. Per stroke:
+   - the rapid to the stroke's place is written as for any toolpath;
+   - DRILL_BANK_PATTERN once per spindle that drills in the stroke: select it;
+   - DRILL_BANK_EXTEND_DRILL once per such spindle: lower it ready to drill;
+   - the plunge, dwell and retract moves of the stroke;
+   - DRILL_BANK_RETRACT_DRILL once per such spindle: raise it again.
+ SETUP_DRILL_BANK is written once per toolpath for every spindle that drills
+ anywhere in it (before the first move), FINAL_DRILL_BANK_ACTION once after the
+ toolpath's last stroke; both are optional. Tags inside these blocks:
+   [DB]  spindle number (1 = leftmost of the row; the column follows the row)
+   [DBX] [DBY] spindle place relative to the reference spindle, mm
+   [DL]  the spindle's hole depth below the start depth, mm
+   [CD]  the spindle's drill diameter, mm
+ A post without PATTERN, EXTEND and RETRACT refuses a drill bank toolpath.
+ ---------------------------------------------------------------------------

POST_NAME = "Drill bank sample (LinuxCNC, mm) (*.ngc)"
FILE_EXTENSION = "ngc"
UNITS = "MM"
LINE_ENDING = "[10]"
SUBSTITUTE = "([)]"

+ Variables: VAR NAME = [tag|mode|prefix|format|multiplier]
VAR TOOL_NUMBER = [T|A||1.0]
VAR SPINDLE_SPEED = [S|A| S|1.0]
VAR FEED_RATE = [F|C| F|1.0]
VAR X_POSITION = [X|C| X|1.3]
VAR Y_POSITION = [Y|C| Y|1.3]
VAR Z_POSITION = [Z|C| Z|1.3]
VAR ARC_CENTRE_I = [I|A| I|1.3]
VAR ARC_CENTRE_J = [J|A| J|1.3]
VAR SAFE_Z = [SAFEZ|A| Z|1.3]
VAR HOME_X = [XH|A| X|1.3]
VAR HOME_Y = [YH|A| Y|1.3]
VAR DWELL_TIME = [DWELL|A| P|1.2]
VAR SPINDLE_NUMBER = [DB|A| P|1.0]
VAR SPINDLE_DX = [DBX|A| I|1.3]
VAR SPINDLE_DY = [DBY|A| J|1.3]
VAR SPINDLE_DEPTH = [DL|A| L|1.3]
VAR SPINDLE_DIAMETER = [CD|A| D|1.3]

begin HEADER
"([TP_FILENAME])"
"(Generated by [PRODUCT])"
"G17 G40 G49 G80 G90 G91.1 G94 G21"
"(Tool [T]: [TOOLNAME])"
"T[T] M6"
"G43 H[T]"
"G0[SAFEZ]"
"([TOOLPATH_NAME])"
"M3[S]"
end

+ Each further toolpath with a different tool.
begin TOOLCHANGE
"M5"
"G0[SAFEZ]"
"(Tool [T]: [TOOLNAME])"
"T[T] M6"
"G43 H[T]"
"G0[SAFEZ]"
"([TOOLPATH_NAME])"
end

begin SPINDLE_ON
"M3[S]"
end

+ Before a toolpath that runs with the spindle off (diamond drag engraving):
+ stop the spindle, lift to safe Z and pause so the operator can check that the
+ spindle is stopped or locked; after the pause lift to safe Z again (Z may have
+ been re-zeroed). The spindle start lines of HEADER, TOOLCHANGE and NEW_SEGMENT
+ are left out for such a toolpath and SPINDLE_ON is not written.
begin SPINDLE_OFF_PAUSE
"M5"
"G0[SAFEZ]"
"(Spindle stays off for diamond drag tool [T]: [TOOLNAME])"
"(Check that the spindle is stopped or locked, then resume)"
"M0"
"G0[SAFEZ]"
end

+ After the last spindle-off toolpath of a drag section, before a toolpath that
+ starts the spindle again: pause so the operator can unlock the spindle.
begin SPINDLE_UNLOCK_PAUSE
"M5"
"G0[SAFEZ]"
"(Diamond drag tool [T] done: unlock the spindle before it starts again)"
"M0"
"G0[SAFEZ]"
end

+ A further toolpath with the same tool.
begin NEW_SEGMENT
"([TOOLPATH_NAME])"
"M3[S]"
end

begin RAPID_MOVE
"G0[X][Y][Z]"
end

begin FEED_MOVE
"G1[X][Y][Z][F]"
end

begin PLUNGE_MOVE
"G1[X][Y][Z][F]"
end

begin RETRACT_MOVE
"G0[Z]"
end

begin CW_ARC_MOVE
"G2[X][Y][Z][I][J][F]"
end

begin CCW_ARC_MOVE
"G3[X][Y][Z][I][J][F]"
end

begin DWELL_MOVE
"G4[DWELL]"
end

+ Once per toolpath, per spindle that drills in it: declare the spindle (its
+ place relative to the reference spindle, its hole depth and drill diameter).
begin SETUP_DRILL_BANK
"(Drill bank spindle[DB][DBX][DBY][CD][DL])"
"M100[DB][DBX][DBY][CD][DL]"
end

+ Per stroke, per spindle: select it for this stroke.
begin DRILL_BANK_PATTERN
"M101[DB]"
end

+ Per stroke, per spindle: lower the spindle's drill (it stops at its depth).
begin DRILL_BANK_EXTEND_DRILL
"M102[DB][DL]"
end

+ Per stroke, per spindle: raise it again after the stroke's last retract.
begin DRILL_BANK_RETRACT_DRILL
"M103[DB]"
end

+ After the toolpath's last stroke.
begin FINAL_DRILL_BANK_ACTION
"M104"
end

begin FOOTER
"G0[SAFEZ]"
"M5"
"G0[XH][YH]"
"M2"
end
